    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_146f5c8c2fb2cb5baec4dae6%3Asnapshot%3A692e6e06c04629d67edf",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The toponyms Kourniachto, Kleftolimano, Fygou, Fylakio, Vardia, Tourkolimnionas, Pano and Kato Maneta are probably the living remnants of pirate activity in the past.",
      "properties": {
        "attestation_id": "att_146f5c8c2fb2cb5baec4dae6",
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false,
        "assertion_class": "SOURCE_STATEMENT",
        "source_classification": "SECONDARY_SOURCE",
        "model_review": {
          "decision": "FLAGGED",
          "flag": {
            "claim_id": "c-aa8cb7d708abaee03bf3",
            "reason": "The statement attributes the toponyms to pirate activity based on a source that discusses the possibility of such an association. The source mentions that the names might be remnants of pirate activity, but it does not provide direct evidence or citations for each toponym. The source also notes that the association is conjectural and based on linguistic similarities rather than historical records. The statement does not include specific sources for each toponym, only a general reference to the source text.",
            "decision": "UNCERTAIN"
          },
          "historical_verification": false
        }
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_b3c9776bd837ec4e7e7e4c25",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 1128360, \"end_line\": 12896, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"greek/library_acquisition/bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [335], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 1127969, \"start_line\": 12892}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_0fcb1152aaa8ec831fe9adfff17da942",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 1128360, \"end_line\": 12896, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"greek/library_acquisition/bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [335], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 1127969, \"start_line\": 12892}",
        "exact_excerpt": "\nA series of coastal toponyms documented on maps or utilized in the modern vernacular of Phournoi\nare probably the living remnants of pirate activity in the past: Kourniachto (a place for hiding or lurking),\n­Kleftolimano (harbor of thieves), Fygou (escape), Fylakio (guard-post), Vardia (shift or guard), Tourkolimnionas\n(harbor of the Turks), Pano and Kato Maneta (upper and lower Maneta).",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_a893d14ba4049826d143f825%3Asnapshot%3A639536d699ae0a17b1c3",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The source mentions the Ottoman Empire and its Barbary corsairs as a common enemy of Malta and Russia.",
      "properties": {
        "attestation_id": "att_a893d14ba4049826d143f825",
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false,
        "assertion_class": "SOURCE_STATEMENT",
        "source_classification": "SECONDARY_SOURCE",
        "model_review": {
          "decision": "SUPPORTED_ATTRIBUTION",
          "flag": null,
          "historical_verification": false
        }
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_c530be5d833cd414b9a3854e",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 494, \"end_line\": 13, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"travellers/library_acquisition/87fd9f63375a2cc4416f2e8c.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 170, \"start_line\": 9}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_46510fe8497f965d4beca00622c32853",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 494, \"end_line\": 13, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"travellers/library_acquisition/87fd9f63375a2cc4416f2e8c.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 170, \"start_line\": 9}",
        "exact_excerpt": " It was the Ottoman Empire, its Muslim Turks, and\nits Barbary corsairs. Unlike Malta, a central Mediterranean archipelago\nwith well-protected, deep-water harbours, Russia had been a largely\nlandlocked country whose territorial expansion historically had tended\nto be across internal frontiers, from Kiev to Muscovy to Kazan.",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_1b9e13bc467d6fad476506c3%3Asnapshot%3A64e2740859b92042fb4a",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The source states that Russia began to nurture a naval and maritime policy after acquiring the Black Sea port of Azov in 1696.",
      "properties": {
        "attestation_id": "att_1b9e13bc467d6fad476506c3",
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false,
        "assertion_class": "SOURCE_STATEMENT",
        "source_classification": "SECONDARY_SOURCE",
        "model_review": {
          "decision": "SUPPORTED_ATTRIBUTION",
          "flag": null,
          "historical_verification": false
        }
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_2b36240ec9d9cb3e436a436f",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 702, \"end_line\": 16, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"travellers/library_acquisition/87fd9f63375a2cc4416f2e8c.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 494, \"start_line\": 13}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_46510fe8497f965d4beca00622c32853",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 702, \"end_line\": 16, \"offset_unit\": \"UNICODE_CODE_POINTS\", \"pdf_file\": \"travellers/library_acquisition/87fd9f63375a2cc4416f2e8c.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0], \"span_semantics\": \"EXACT_QUOTE\", \"start_char\": 494, \"start_line\": 13}",
        "exact_excerpt": " With the\nadvent of Peter I, however, and especially after his declaration of war\nagainst Turkey and the acquisition of the Black Sea port of Azov in 1696,\nRussia began to nurture a naval and maritime policy.",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
